1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
If your leadership team agreed fast and everyone

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
felt good about it, be careful.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,750
Comfortable consensus usually isn't alignment.

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:14,150
It's groupthink — the drive for harmony quietly

5
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:18,000
overriding a real look at the alternatives.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,556
The danger isn't that people disagree and hide

7
00:00:21,556 --> 00:00:22,000
it.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,556
It's that they stop generating the disagreement at

9
00:00:25,556 --> 00:00:26,000
all.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,556
The room gets smooth, and smooth rooms miss

11
00:00:29,556 --> 00:00:30,000
things.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
The fix isn't hoping someone speaks up.

13
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,571
It's assigning it.

14
00:00:33,571 --> 00:00:36,429
Give one person the job of arguing the

15
00:00:36,429 --> 00:00:39,286
other side — make dissent a role, not

16
00:00:39,286 --> 00:00:40,000
a personality.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
In your last big decision — who was

18
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
actually responsible for arguing against it?
